1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:07,939
PQ PayGuard turns a quantum exposure score into a binding payment decision on QDay Aevum chain 44005.

2
00:00:08,109 --> 00:00:13,343
Dashboards leave that score as passive metadata. Here it selects the on chain release path.

3
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:20,981
The contract maps every score to a gate, instant release through full quarantine, and the commitment binds the score before funds move.

4
00:00:21,601 --> 00:00:24,795
The additive model rates the receiving signature scheme.

5
00:00:24,965 --> 00:00:32,209
A post quantum scheme like ML DSA, or SLH DSA from the SPHINCS plus family, sits in the low tier.

6
00:00:32,379 --> 00:00:36,847
RSA 2048 with a revealed key climbs into the critical band.

7
00:00:37,017 --> 00:00:42,728
Every change recomputes the attestation hash, the keccak commitment and the createEscrow calldata.

8
00:00:43,348 --> 00:00:48,053
The simulator mirrors the contract, same gate order and same revert names.

9
00:00:48,222 --> 00:00:54,471
The payer opens a session policy with per escrow and cumulative velocity caps, delays and a guardian.

10
00:00:54,641 --> 00:01:01,269
A low score releases instantly; a medium score sits under the session timelock, so an early release reverts.

11
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:06,797
Warp the clock past the delay and it pays out, and the payer can still revoke inside the window.

12
00:01:07,416 --> 00:01:11,192
The high tier adds a guardian co-sign on top of a longer delay.

13
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:15,720
One guardian approval registers, then the timelock still has to pass.

14
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:21,870
Critical is quarantined. Release always reverts and the payer reclaims, all of it in the audit trail.

15
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:28,753
Six live attacks fire at the same code. Signature replay dies on consumed nonce ids and actor checks.

16
00:01:28,923 --> 00:01:35,132
Domain forgery, one time leaf reuse, merkle tampering and the limit bypass all fail closed.

17
00:01:35,302 --> 00:01:41,052
The toy Shor drain breaks the classical key in the open, while the commit protected path stays safe.

18
00:01:41,222 --> 00:01:46,492
Every verdict is computed live, the same defenses the Foundry suite proves on bytecode.

19
00:01:47,112 --> 00:01:52,776
Receipts are signed with a WOTS plus merkle wallet, the hash family that SPHINCS plus is built on.

20
00:01:52,945 --> 00:01:59,349
Build and sign, and the receipt verifies. Verify a tampered copy, and detection is explicit.

21
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:06,683
The in page battery adds SHA 256 and keccak known answers, round trips, proofs and bookmarks.

22
00:02:07,303 --> 00:02:14,160
Nothing is asserted without a check. 274 JavaScript tests, including real Anvil EVM parity.

23
00:02:14,330 --> 00:02:21,115
100 Foundry tests cover units, fuzz, invariants and reentrancy. 374 passing.

24
00:02:21,285 --> 00:02:28,126
The testnet panel stays opt in. The probe reads chain id and block number live, falling back to a marked simulation.

25
00:02:28,296 --> 00:02:35,451
The scripted qday preflight gates the one command deploy across env, key, toolchain, chain id, balance.

26
00:02:35,620 --> 00:02:40,877
No mainnet transaction is claimed anywhere. PQ PayGuard. The score is the gate.
